<%# locals: (named_url:, format:, colors:, unit_factor:, thumbnail:, thumbnail_url:, download_url:, name:) %>
<%# Interactive client-side 3D viewer (Online3DViewer), see modelviewer_controller.js. `lazy`
    gates the byte fetch AND the ~1 MB engine download behind the "View in 3D" button, so
    nothing heavy loads unless the user asks. The fallback (thumbnail poster + download) is the
    resting state and also the graceful-degradation target if the viewer can't boot.

    A NAMED URL, NOT A PLAIN ONE, and it is load-bearing exactly as it is for the KiCanvas embed:
    Online3DViewer chooses an importer from the URL'S OWN trailing extension, never from the bytes
    or a Content-Type, so a path with no extension in it reaches no importer at all
    (docs/invariants/files-preview.md). `named_url` is the caller's, because the maker's page names
    /files/:id/blob/:name and a visitor's /u/:handle/:slug/files/:id/:name (stage 4, S4-5). %>
<div class="model-viewer"
     data-controller="modelviewer"
     data-modelviewer-lazy-value="true"
     data-modelviewer-url-value="<%= named_url %>"
     data-modelviewer-format-value="<%= format %>"
     <%# WHAT THE IMPORTER CANNOT READ FOR ITSELF, from Maker::ThreeMfManifest: one slicer
         filament colour per imported mesh, and the millimetre factor for the model's declared
         unit (three's 3MFLoader ignores it, so an Onshape part in metres measures 1000x short).
         Empty and 1 for every other format, which is the no-op the controller checks for. %>
     data-modelviewer-colors-value="<%= colors.to_json %>"
     data-modelviewer-unit-factor-value="<%= unit_factor %>">
  <div class="model-viewer-stage" data-modelviewer-target="canvas"></div>
  <div class="model-viewer-bar">
    <span class="model-viewer-dims" data-modelviewer-target="dims"></span>
    <span class="mv-launch">
      <button type="button" class="btn small" data-action="modelviewer#load">View in 3D</button>
    </span>
    <span class="mv-actions">
      <button type="button" class="btn small ghost" data-action="modelviewer#reset">Reset view</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn small ghost" data-action="modelviewer#fullscreen">Fullscreen</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn small ghost" aria-label="Return to image" data-action="modelviewer#showPoster">✕ Image</button>
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="model-viewer-fallback" data-modelviewer-target="fallback">
    <%# THE POSTER'S URL IS A STRICT LOCAL TOO (hardening, 2026-09-08; tinkerex#278), for
        `named_url`'s reason one comment up plus one of its own: `url_for(thumbnail.asset)` is a blob
        URL with no expiry, so a visitor's poster kept answering after the project went private. %>
    <% if thumbnail&.status == "ready" && thumbnail.asset.attached? %>
      <img src="<%= thumbnail_url %>" alt="Preview of <%= name %>" class="preview-image">
    <% end %>
    <p class="muted">Click <strong>View in 3D</strong> to load an interactive preview, or download the file.</p>
    <%= link_to "Download #{name}", download_url, class: "btn" %>
  </div>
</div>
